  "narrative": "The new validation evidence clarifies the current evidence hierarchy. For the response-deadline claim H37, feature_010=1 versus feature_010=0 was tested in the positive direction; positive signed estimates mean that feature_010=1 has a higher raw outcome_001 value, i.e. weaker dependency. Discovery gave +0.4232 units (R18), and independent validation gave +0.4707 units with independent interval +0.3343 to +0.6071 (R51). Both estimates are far above the 0.15-unit threshold, the validation interval is entirely above threshold, and both comparison cells are adequately large. I therefore reassess H37 as accepted and closed. Together with previously accepted and validated claims for feature_037 and feature_002, and the accepted feature_063 claim, the supplied dataset supports four robust binary associations: feature_037=1 is associated with stronger composite dependency, feature_063=1 is associated with stronger composite dependency, feature_010=1 is associated with weaker dependency, and feature_002=1 is associated with weaker dependency. These remain within-supplied-data associations, not causal, mechanistic, coding-oriented, or generalizable claims.\n\nThe central new question is H95, the clean-context test of feature_003=1 versus feature_003=0 after fixing the four accepted predictors at zero. H95 is direction -1, so positive signed estimates mean feature_003=1 has a more negative raw outcome_001 value, i.e. stronger dependency. Discovery gave +0.1643 units with interval +0.1011 to +0.2275 (R65), and independent validation gave +0.1511 units with independent interval +0.0560 to +0.2461 (R77). The direction is consistently positive across the controlled clean context and the independent validation sample, but the validation point estimate is only marginally above the 0.15-unit threshold and the independent interval remains wide, with lower bounds well below the scientific threshold. Therefore, although the evidence supports a positive direction and perhaps a near-threshold clean-context signal, it does not provide robust evidence for a scientifically meaningful threshold-size effect. I keep H95 unresolved and active rather than accepting it, because the key remaining ambiguity is not direction but whether feature_003 contributes a meaningful effect beyond stronger predictors or only in a narrow predictor-absent context.\n\nThe scheduled validation for H34 closes a residual high-feature_038 subgroup question. H34 tested feature_007=1 versus feature_007=0 within feature_038>=0.75 in the negative direction; positive signed estimates would mean stronger dependency. Discovery was slightly negative in signed terms (-0.0271; R23), and validation was essentially null (+0.0102; R78) with independent interval -0.1634 to +0.1838. Neither estimate is threshold-size, and the validation interval is compatible with both negligible and opposite-sign small effects but not with the claimed threshold-size stronger-dependency effect. I reassess H34 as rejected and closed. This is consistent with the broader pattern that the constructed research markers and signature-defined subgroups do not supply robust outcome_001 associations.\n\nOther negative findings remain informative. Feature_060 tested in clean and single-predictor-controlled contexts showed no threshold-size stronger-dependency evidence, and the small opposite-direction estimates do not justify a separate threshold-level claim; I consider that line closed unless a new precise reverse-direction hypothesis emerges. Exploratory broad categorical contrasts for feature_024 and feature_046 are below threshold and closed. The constructed markers feature_007, feature_058, and feature_015 also remain non-supportive as broad predictors.\n\nThe most informative next analysis is a context-dependence test for feature_003. I registered an interaction hypothesis, linked to H95, comparing the feature_003 contrast in the clean all-zero context feature_002=0/feature_037=0/feature_010=0/feature_063=0 with its complement. This asks whether the near-threshold clean-context feature_003 estimate exceeds the feature_003 estimate in contexts where at least one accepted predictor is present. If this interaction is threshold-size and coherent, the defensible conclusion would be context-specific feature_003 association, not a broad main effect. If it is null or imprecise, I would close H95 and treat feature_003 as a near-threshold supplied-data signal rather than a distinct predictor association. Across all conclusions, the strongest supported findings remain the four validated feature_037, feature_063, feature_010, and feature_002 associations, with feature_003 unresolved near threshold.",
  "research_notes": "Synthesis update after H37 response deadline, H95 validation, and H34 validation. Accepted robust within-supplied-data associations remain: H24 feature_037=1 stronger dependency; H27 feature_063=1 stronger dependency; H37 feature_010=1 weaker dependency; H63 feature_002=1 weaker dependency. H37 validation +0.4707 [0.3343,0.6071] confirms. H34 feature_007 high feature_038 subgroup validated null and closed: discovery -0.0271, validation +0.0102 [-0.1634,0.1838]; no threshold-size evidence. H95 clean-context feature_003 direction -1: discovery +0.1643 [0.1011,0.2275], validation +0.1511 [0.0560,0.2461]. Direction positive and validation point just above threshold, but intervals include subthreshold values and validation lower bound is far below threshold; keep H95 unresolved/active. The next most informative test is the newly registered interaction comparing clean-context feature_003 effect with complement feature_003 effect (subgroup feature_002=0/feature_037=0/feature_010=0/feature_063=0). If interaction threshold-size and direction-coherent, consider only a context-specific feature_003 conclusion, not a broad association; if not, close H95/feature_003 line. Feature_060 closed: clean and controlled conditional tests are null or small opposite-direction, no threshold-size. Feature_024 and feature_046 broad categorical contrasts closed. Negative broad-marker findings remain stable. All claims remain associations in the supplied dataset only, not causal, mechanistic, coding, or generalizable."
